AND THE CLOSED-DOMAIN CASE (finding 2): a wall boundary gives bit-zero
boundary phi, so the boundary-only denominator is EXACTLY ZERO and
relativeDeparture returns 0.0 by its scale<=0 arm, whatever the interior
flux or the scatter did.
    interior 1e6, boundary 0.0
    artifact                  0.000000e+00   (NON-ZERO: the real artifact)
    mine  (boundary denom)    0.000000e+00   <- reported, and it cannot read false
    ADR-071 (all-faces denom) 0.000000e+00   <- what it should be
